is on "spiking" phenomena</article-title><source>Clin Biochem</source><year>1997</year><volume>30</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9056110</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B23"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Pentheroudakis</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><article-title>The neutrophil, not the tumor: serum CA 15-3 elevation as a result of granulocyte&#x02013;colony-stimulating factor-induced neutrophil MU1C overexpression and neutrophilia in patients with breast carcinoma receiving adjuvant chemotherapy</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>2004</year><volume>101</volume><issue>8</issue><fpage>1767</fpage><lpage>75</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15386335</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B24"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Colomer</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><article-title>Circulating CA 15-3 levels in the postsurgical follow-up of breast cancer patients and in non-malignant diseases</article-title><source>Breast Cancer Res Treat</source><year>1989</year><volume>13</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>123</fpage><lpage>33</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2730960</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B25"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Hashimoto</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsubara</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><article-title>Changes in the tumor marker concentration in female patients with hyper-, eu-, and hypothyroidism</article-title><source>Endocrinol Jpn</source><year>1989</year><volume>36</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>873</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2483831</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B26"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Symeonidis</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><article-title>Increased serum CA-15.3 levels in patients with megaloblastic anemia due to vitamin B12 defic